{"id":98900756851143,"type":"album","name":"Up On The Sun","artist":"Meat Puppets","year":1985,"weight":13,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711009.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-ee69978f-bd5c-400d-84a8-5f15bab438e4/mbid-ee69978f-bd5c-400d-84a8-5f15bab438e4-13542382890.jpg","scaruffi":7.5,"yt":"i6pzaRulgg0","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/5obGGGs1Gcf4gJzCte6iJf","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_m5E63Q8YPMjN-JbEMK91qvOhfScH5fHFg","bandcamp":"https://meatpuppets.bandcamp.com/album/up-on-the-sun"},"desc":"Up on the Sun is the third album by the Meat Puppets, released on March 21, 1985, by SST Records. The album features a cleaner and more technical sound with a more psychedelic rock feel, in contrast to the sloppy punk approach of their first album (1982), while continuing with the mystical, poetic lyrics and country-inflected songwriting of Meat Puppets II (1984). Brothers Curt and Cris Kirkwood were interested in psychedelic rock. The pair often indulged in recreational drug use with Derrick Bostrom, who came from an affluent, politically liberal family in Arizona and who introduced them to punk rock. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":255331505881484,"name":"The Meat Puppets","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/MeatPuppetsHi-ToneMemphis.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":114184582437226,"type":"genre","name":"Cowpunk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":225077317735581,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Cowpunk","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":2,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":7.5},{"id":52032266791182,"name":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":167,"year":null,"note":null,"total":877,"scaruffi":7.5}],"podcast":[],"book_tracks":[{"id":98900756851143,"artist":"Meat Pu